Do not add fake loading delays.

Animation requirements

Use restrained, purposeful animations:

- Short screen transitions.
- Smooth drawer opening and closing.
- Subtle button press feedback.
- Tab and selection transitions.
- Progress-bar animation when progress changes.
- Skeleton shimmer only while content is loading.
- Small modal and dropdown transitions.
- Natural expansion and collapse of curriculum modules.

Prefer CSS transitions or a lightweight animation library.

Keep most micro-interactions around 120–220ms when appropriate. Avoid long page transitions.

Respect "prefers-reduced-motion".

Animations must never block navigation or make the app feel sluggish.

Flicker and layout stability

Prevent:

- White flashes between route changes.
- Content jumping after images load.
- Navigation bars moving unexpectedly.
- Repeated loading indicators during stable data.
- Flashing between authenticated and unauthenticated screens.
- Duplicate requests caused by unnecessary component remounts.
- Skeletons appearing briefly when cached content is already available.

Maintain consistent layouts and render stable fallbacks while data loads.

